        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iranian leaders 'do not take any statements from Donald Trump seriously ' Middle East Issued on: 30/03/2026 - 12:47 The United States and Israel kept up their attacks on March 30 on the Islamic Republic, even as there were signs of progress in nascent ceasefire talks. But according to FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah, based in Tehran, Iranian authorities do not take statements from Trump seriously. He also tells us about strikes on the capital city. Donald Trump has also suggested that the US could take Iran's Kharg Island, which would be difficult to hold and 'with no guarantees that it'll work.' Thousands of Lebanese trapped behind Israeli frontlines rely on humanitarian aid 30/03/2026 Middle East Occupying Iran's Kharg island could be 'dangerous and risky' for US forces 30/03/2026 Middle East ‘Transnational repression’: Iranian diaspora faces harassment, death threats, pressure on families 30/03/2026 Middle East New Israeli defence budget 'another indication of breach between people and government' 30/03/2026 Middle East Israel, US and Iran exchange airstrikes despite attempted talks 30/03/2026 Middle East What do we know about the failed bomb attack against Bank of America in Paris? 30/03/2026 Middle East 30/03/2026 Middle East Trump wants to 'take oil' in Iran as 'tit-for-tat violence' continues 30/03/2026 Middle East Israeli police bar top Catholic figure in Jerusalem from holding Palm Sunday mass at Holy Sepulchre 29/03/2026 Middle East"
